.shots/
node_modules/
.settings.json

# Coverage output: c8 puts raw V8 data and HTML here. It is generated on demand
# by `npm run coverage` and one CI step, and lives only until the next run.
coverage/

# Landing build for Cloudflare Pages, generated on their side.
_site/

# What install.sh downloads, built by tools/dist.mjs from a tag. It lives on
# the release page, never in the tree: a tarball per version in the history
# would be a megabyte forever for bytes git can already reproduce.
dist/

# Third-party modules under modules/ are private, live in their own repository,
# and arrive here through a symlink. Core neither stores nor notices them:
# otherwise they would appear in every connected checkout's status and one day
# be added here just to silence it.
/modules/*
!/modules/radio/
!/modules/plan/
!/modules/polaroid/
!/modules/newsstand/

# The agent rulebook is not committed. It entered the tree on 3 September 2026
# for a valid reason: worktrees contain only tracked files, so an agent on a new
# branch started from nothing. The owner reversed that decision on 5 September:
# rules describe the team, not the office, and cloning core must not silently
# impose somebody else's practice. Worktrees are solved without a commit: files
# are copied into new trees from the list below, while an installer voluntarily
# puts agents, synchronisation, and routines into a new clone. The paid rulebook
# module will bring it automatically; the open build keeps it optional.
#
# These files remain on disk and work; they simply stay untracked.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.githooks/

# How these files reach a worktree: `.worktreeinclude` tells Claude Code which
# ignored files to copy when creating one. Verified on 4 September 2026 in a new
# worktree: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, and .githooks/pre-commit arrive byte-for-byte,
# the hook keeps its executable bit, and git status stays clean because copies
# remain ignored.
#
# The list itself is ignored: it names exactly what appears above, and committing
# it would return to the repository what was removed on 4 September.
#
# This is a copy, not a link: changing AGENTS.md in the main checkout does not
# update existing worktrees, or vice versa. `.githooks/` is listed because
# core.hooksPath is relative and finds hooks beside itself, one copy per tree.
# `.claude/` as a whole is excluded because it contains the worktrees themselves.
.worktreeinclude

# Core's backlog follows for the same reason. Created on 3 September 2026, it
# was removed on the 5th: planning belongs in the private repository with the
# other internal documents, as decided when the repositories split. Two lists
# for one project drift silently, and people mistake the visible one for complete.
BACKLOG.md

# Video draft written by release.mjs on every minor release. It is deliberately
# untracked: material for a person, not product output. Generated debris once
# blocked the next release because the script rejects dirty trees; after v0.4.0
# on 5 September 2026 its own output became the uncommitted change blocking it.
media/

# Rulebook backups left by merge tools and other sessions, such as
# `AGENTS.md.orig` and `AGENTS.md.before-pushing-…`. AGENTS.md is ignored, so its
# copies must be too; otherwise they appear in another status and stop releases.
AGENTS.md.*
CLAUDE.md.*
